    "narrative": "Our lineup for July 26 centers on **Dylan Beavers** and **Geraldo Perdomo**, who emerge as our strongest plays today with scores of 68.38 and 68.19, respectively. **Dylan Beavers** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a favorable matchup against the right-handed Reynaldo L\u00f3pez, combined with the premium lead-off spot. Similarly, **Geraldo Perdomo** is primed to capitalize on a soft matchup against Miles Mikolas (4.71 xERA) and the elevated efficiency of hitting second in the order. **Bryce Harper** remains a \"Strong\" start at 67.44; despite the lineup pending designation, his elite xwOBA metrics and favorable park conditions make him an automatic lock in the three-hole, regardless of the opposing right-hander Will Warren.\n\nStrategic shifts were dictated heavily by the scarcity of stolen bases and park-adjusted efficiency. **Taylor Ward** (64.51) and **Luis Arraez** (60.52) provide necessary balance, with **Luis Arraez** bolstered by a significant wind advantage (+5%) and his traditional high-order usage. We are closely monitoring the **Daulton Varsho** situation; while his score of 47.78 is modest due to a platoon disadvantage against a left-handed pitcher, his specific profile\u2014an elite sprint speed threat against a pitcher with a notoriously slow delivery\u2014gives him a tactical edge in our pursuit of stolen bases that pure projection models might underestimate. **Cal Raleigh** remains in the lineup despite a tough draw against Jacob deGrom (3.07 xERA), as his base projection remains too high to bench, even with the projected skill drain.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **JJ Bleday** (46.72), who narrowly missed the final cut. While his underlying metrics are solid, he was squeezed out by the sheer volume of high-ceiling options and a negative platoon adjustment against a right-handed starter, which pushed his efficiency below the required threshold to displace our lower-scoring outfielders. Conversely, we are keeping a close watch on **Gleyber Torres**, who carries a 57.51 score; despite a notable -13% platoon hit, his current park factor and the weakness of the opposing arm keep him viable in the utility spot. We have confirmed that **Tyler Freeman** is out of the starting lineup today, so he remains firmly on the bench to preserve our game caps.",
